# Angular frontend

Read `docs/ANGULAR-GUIDE.md` before changing frontend code.

- Project is Angular 20.3: standalone is default; keep explicit
  `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush`; do not introduce Angular 22-only APIs.
- Page/container owns route, permissions, API orchestration and page state.
- Presentational component uses `input()`/`output()`/`model()`, owns only local UI
  state, and does not inject domain API services, Router or product store.
- Split only at a real responsibility/state/test boundary. File size triggers review,
  never mechanical extraction or forwarding wrappers.
- Signals for synchronous local state; `computed()` for derived state; `effect()` only
  for side effects. RxJS remains for HTTP/async composition with bounded teardown.
- Raw `HttpClient` in components, mutable inputs, nested subscriptions, new `any`,
  `NgModule`, `ngClass/ngStyle`, `*ngIf/*ngFor`, and cross-page imports are forbidden.
- Typed Reactive Forms remain canon; do not add Signal Forms or new dependencies.
- Preserve SilentResult services, Paper & Ink tokens, keyboard/focus and light/dark.
- Refactor in small behavior-preserving batches. Add characterization tests before
  changing ambiguous legacy behavior.
- Required gates: frontend tsc, focused Jest, changed-file ESLint,
  `pnpm architecture:check`, `git diff --check`, and browser smoke for UI paths.
